---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DocNav from '../components/DocNav.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy — Prabal Banerjee"
  description="Privacy notice for prabalbanerjee.xyz: what this static personal site collects, the third parties involved, and how to avoid them."
>
  <div class="terminal-content">
    <DocNav current="privacy" />

    <main>
      <section id="privacy" class="doc">
        <h1 class="sr-only">Privacy notice</h1>
        <div class="terminal-prompt-line" aria-hidden="true">$ cat privacy.txt</div>

        <p>
          This is a personal website. It is a set of static files — there is no application server, no
          database, no account system, no shopping cart and no form anywhere on it. I do not ask you
          for your name, your email address or anything else, and there is nothing here for you to log
          in to.
        </p>

        <h2>What the site itself collects</h2>
        <p>
          Nothing directly. The pages set no cookies of their own and store nothing in your browser
          beyond the ordinary HTTP cache. Because the site is served from a static host, that host
          keeps the usual web server request logs — IP address, user agent, requested path, timestamp —
          which I do not have any special access to and do not use.
        </p>

        <h2>Third parties</h2>
        <p>
          Two third parties see your request, and you should know about both.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Google Analytics.</strong> Every page loads Google Analytics (property
          UA-97017425-1) to count visits. It sets its own cookies and reports page views, approximate
          location and device information back to Google. If you would rather not be counted, any
          content blocker or the Google Analytics opt-out add-on will stop it, and the site works
          exactly the same without it.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Google Fonts.</strong> Typefaces are requested from fonts.googleapis.com and
          fonts.gstatic.com, which means Google sees your IP address and user agent when a page loads.
        </p>
        <p>
          Links out to X, GitHub, LinkedIn, arXiv, publishers and other sites are ordinary links.
          Once you follow one you are on somebody else's site under somebody else's privacy policy.
        </p>

        <h2>Automated clients</h2>
        <p>
          Crawlers and AI agents are welcome. <a href="/robots.txt">/robots.txt</a> allows everything,
          <a href="/sitemap-index.xml">/sitemap-index.xml</a> lists every page, and
          <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> is a plain-text summary of the site written for machine
          readers. Nothing here is behind a paywall, a login or a rate limit.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
        <p>
          If this notice changes, the change ships with the site and is visible in its public
          <a href="https://github.com/prabal-banerjee/prabal-banerjee.github.io">source repository</a>,
          which is the authoritative history of what this page has said. Questions about any of the
          above can go to the contact addresses listed on the
          <a href="/#contact">home page</a>.
        </p>

        <p class="back"><a href="/">&larr; back to the terminal</a></p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .doc {
    max-width: 900px;
  }

  .doc p {
    color: var(--subtext);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    max-width: 72ch;
  }

  .doc h2 {
    color: var(--mauve);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 2rem 0 0.8rem;
  }

  .doc .back {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }
</style>
